course: dictionary
lesson: 13643
title: Inexpensive: cheap in a good way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inexpensive means not costing a lot of money. «We bought an inexpensive gift for Gran's birthday.» The clue is the word gift: it is a low-cost present, and it is still a nice thing to give.
explain: Look at the word parts. In- means not, and expensive means costing a lot, so inexpensive means not expensive. «The café serves inexpensive lunches, so we eat there every Friday.» They keep going back, so the lunches must be good value.
explain: Cheap can mean low price, but it can also mean poor quality, like a toy that breaks in a day. Inexpensive usually has no bad feeling about quality. «These inexpensive trainers are light and comfy» tells you the price is low and the shoes are still good. Ask yourself: is the writer being polite or rude about the price?
fact: Inexpensive means not costing a lot of money.
fact: Inexpensive is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «an inexpensive gift».
fact: The adverb is inexpensively: «We shopped inexpensively this week.»
fact: The prefix in- means not, so inexpensive is the opposite of expensive.
fact: Cheap can mean poor quality as well as low price; inexpensive usually does not.
exercise: «We bought an inexpensive gift for Gran.» What does inexpensive mean? | Very large and heavy | Made of real gold | Very expensive and fancy | *Not costing a lot of money
exercise: «The café serves inexpensive lunches.» Which word is the opposite of inexpensive? | Cheap | Quiet | *Expensive | Tiny
exercise: «We can shop inexpensively at the market.» Find and copy the adverb. | market | can | *inexpensively | shop
test: «Our class found an inexpensive way to have fun: a picnic in the park.» Why is a picnic called inexpensive? | It takes all day | It needs a big stage | It is very noisy | *It costs very little money
test: Which sentence uses inexpensive in a polite, positive way? | *«These inexpensive trainers are light and comfy.» | This bag is cheap and rubbish. | Those cheap cards were all torn. | The shop sold cheap junk that broke in a day.
exam: «The inexpensive restaurant was full on Friday night.» What does inexpensive mean here? | Closed for the night | Very tall and grand | *Not costing much money | Dark and quiet
